==English==

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|theoretical|-ly|id2=adverbial}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-theoretically.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-theoretically.wav|a=US}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# [[in theory]]; [[on paper]]
#: {{ux|en|I haven't tested it, but '''theoretically''' it ought to fly.}}
# in a [[theoretical]] manner
#: {{ux|en|I solved the problem '''theoretically''' rather than practically.}}
# [[in theory]] though not necessarily in reality.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=14 Dec 85|volume=13|number=22|journal=Gay Community News|page=10|author=Gordon Gottlieb|title=L.A. Community Divided over Terrigno Indictment|text=Rumors of an indictment had spread through this heavily gay and lesbian community since shortly after the '''theoretically''' secret investigation began in 1984.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|date=November 1, 2023|title=[https://www.youtube.com/shorts/bbhneLqGsYw Honest Dentist Appointment]|passage=No, but insurance does cover it. '''Theoretically'''.}}

